GFOpenTorrent: no query filter on AmigaOS, so no console for it.
PicoTorrent's query language (PQL) runs on the ANTLR4 C++ runtime, which
is not in the tree; compat/picotorrent/pqltorrentfilter_amiga.cpp (copied
over ui/filters/pqltorrentfilter.cpp by the build) gives no filter and
says why. MainFrame keeps the console that takes queries hidden and its
View menu item off. Under __WXOPENLAYOUT__, Windows' code as it was.
